## What Problem This Solves

Auto-recall selectivity in `memory-lancedb` is hardcoded: minimum similarity
score 0.3, candidate overfetch 10, injection cap 3. Operators cannot tune
precision/recall for their own data without editing plugin source.

## What This Does

Surfaces the three knobs as plugin config, with manifest `uiHints` and defaults
equal to the previous hardcoded values:

| Setting               | Default | Range | Applies to                                    |
| --------------------- | ------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------- |
| `recallMinScore`      | `0.3`   | 0–1   | Minimum similarity for auto-recall injection. |
| `autoRecallOverfetch` | `10`    | 1–200 | Candidate pool fetched before scoring/capping. |
| `recallResultCap`     | `3`     | 1–50  | Maximum memories injected per turn.           |

The values are threaded through the live-config merge, so operator settings
take effect at the `before_prompt_build` hook — not only at startup. **Behavior
is unchanged when unset.**

**Validation parity (review follow-up):** the two count settings are declared
`integer` in the manifest, and the runtime parser rejects — rather than
silently floors — non-integer values for them, so a config can never validate
in one layer and be reinterpreted by the other. A parity test pins both layers
to the same types, bounds, and failure modes. `recallResultCap` raises only the
injected block size when explicitly configured; the docs now carry a
prompt-budget note for elevated caps, and `autoRecallOverfetch` never increases
injected content (it only widens the internal candidate pool).

Extracted from #108782 following its review's recommendation to split this
tuning improvement from the partitioning contract; the two PRs are independent
(whichever lands second trivially rebases one shared call site).

## Evidence

**Real-behavior proof** — real pinned `@lancedb/lancedb` driver on an on-disk
table (no mocks), replaying `MemoryDB.search()`'s exact behavior (agent-fenced
`vectorSearch().where().limit(<overfetch>)`, `score = 1/(1+distance)`, minScore
filter, injection-cap slice) with default vs non-default settings.
Deterministic vectors, no network:

<details>
<summary>Proof output + reproducible script (drop at repo root, <code>node _thresholds-proof.mjs</code>)</summary>

```text
temp store: /tmp/mldb-thresholds-proof-XXXXXX

real ANN scores: strong=1.000  medium=0.500  weak=0.338

DEFAULTS — autoRecallOverfetch=10, recallMinScore=0.3, recallResultCap=3
  injected: [strong,medium,weak]
  [PASS] default settings inject all three memories

NON-DEFAULT recallMinScore=0.85 — stricter similarity cutoff
  injected: [strong]
  [PASS] 0.85 cutoff excludes the medium and weak matches

NON-DEFAULT recallResultCap=1 — injection cap
  injected: [strong]
  [PASS] cap=1 injects only the top match despite three passing the cutoff

NON-DEFAULT autoRecallOverfetch=1 — candidate pool reaches the driver
  injected: [strong]
  [PASS] overfetch=1 limits the ANN candidate pool itself to the single nearest row

=== RESULT: ALL CHECKS PASSED ===
```

```js
import { mkdtemp, rm } from "node:fs/promises";
import { tmpdir } from "node:os";
import { join } from "node:path";
import * as lancedb from "@lancedb/lancedb";

// Replays MemoryDB.search()'s exact behavior on the real driver: an
// agent-fenced vectorSearch().where().limit(<overfetch>) followed by
// score = 1/(1+_distance), a minScore filter, then the injection cap slice —
// with default vs non-default selectivity settings.
const AGENT = "main";
const query = [1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0];
const vec = (t) => [1, t, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]; // distance to query grows with t

let failures = 0;
function check(label, cond) {
  console.log(`  [${cond ? "PASS" : "FAIL"}] ${label}`);
  if (!cond) failures++;
}

// The exact math MemoryDB.search applies to driver rows.
async function searchLikeMemoryDB(tbl, { overfetch, minScore, cap }) {
  const rows = await tbl
    .vectorSearch(query)
    .where(`agentId = '${AGENT}'`)
    .limit(overfetch)
    .toArray();
  return rows
    .map((r) => ({ id: r.id, score: 1 / (1 + (r._distance ?? 0)) }))
    .filter((r) => r.score >= minScore)
    .slice(0, cap);
}
const ids = (rows) => rows.map((r) => r.id).join(",");

const dir = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), "mldb-thresholds-proof-"));
console.log(`temp store: ${dir}\n`);

try {
  const db = await lancedb.connect(dir);
  await db.createTable("memories", [
    { id: "strong", text: "prefers dark roast coffee", vector: query, importance: 1, category: "preference", createdAt: 1, agentId: AGENT },
    { id: "medium", text: "sometimes drinks tea", vector: vec(1), importance: 1, category: "fact", createdAt: 2, agentId: AGENT },
    { id: "weak", text: "a loosely related note", vector: vec(1.4), importance: 1, category: "other", createdAt: 3, agentId: AGENT },
  ]);
  const tbl = await db.openTable("memories");

  const scores = await searchLikeMemoryDB(tbl, { overfetch: 10, minScore: 0, cap: 10 });
  console.log("real ANN scores:", scores.map((r) => `${r.id}=${r.score.toFixed(3)}`).join("  "), "\n");

  console.log("DEFAULTS — autoRecallOverfetch=10, recallMinScore=0.3, recallResultCap=3");
  const defaults = await searchLikeMemoryDB(tbl, { overfetch: 10, minScore: 0.3, cap: 3 });
  console.log(`  injected: [${ids(defaults)}]`);
  check("default settings inject all three memories", ids(defaults) === "strong,medium,weak");

  console.log("\nNON-DEFAULT recallMinScore=0.85 — stricter similarity cutoff");
  const strict = await searchLikeMemoryDB(tbl, { overfetch: 10, minScore: 0.85, cap: 3 });
  console.log(`  injected: [${ids(strict)}]`);
  check("0.85 cutoff excludes the medium and weak matches", ids(strict) === "strong");

  console.log("\nNON-DEFAULT recallResultCap=1 — injection cap");
  const capped = await searchLikeMemoryDB(tbl, { overfetch: 10, minScore: 0.3, cap: 1 });
  console.log(`  injected: [${ids(capped)}]`);
  check("cap=1 injects only the top match despite three passing the cutoff", ids(capped) === "strong");

  console.log("\nNON-DEFAULT autoRecallOverfetch=1 — candidate pool reaches the driver");
  const pooled = await searchLikeMemoryDB(tbl, { overfetch: 1, minScore: 0.3, cap: 3 });
  console.log(`  injected: [${ids(pooled)}]`);
  check("overfetch=1 limits the ANN candidate pool itself to the single nearest row", ids(pooled) === "strong");

  console.log(`\n=== RESULT: ${failures === 0 ? "ALL CHECKS PASSED" : failures + " CHECK(S) FAILED"} ===`);
} finally {
  await rm(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
process.exit(failures === 0 ? 0 : 1);
```

</details>

**Automated checks**

- `pnpm test:extension memory-lancedb` — **148 tests passing**, including:
  a regression test proving configured values survive the live-config merge
  into auto-recall (an overfetch of 4 and a minScore of 0.85 reach the search
  instead of being silently dropped and reparsed as defaults once a live
  runtime config object is present, which is the normal case); and a
  manifest/runtime **validation-parity test** (fractional counts rejected by
  both layers, identical bounds, boundary values preserved verbatim).
- `tsgo` prod + test lanes, the type-aware extensions lint shard, the
  type-suppression inventory, and the docs format/map checks are all green.

## What To Review

- The strict integer resolver and validation ranges
  (`extensions/memory-lancedb/config.ts`) and the matching manifest `integer`
  constraints.
- The live-config threading in `resolveCurrentHookConfig` — the fix the
  regression test pins down.

